 procedures, and publicly report data on bullying incidents. The Department of Education would evaluate anti-bullying programs every two years, and the National Center for Education Statistics would collect nationwide data on these incidents.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"School districts, and children in them. Children, and the adults responsible for them.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M000687","score":0.05798866766035882},"overlapCount":178},"meaning":{"percentile":29.316063812983728,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.6209198669944564}},{"billId":"119-hr-7977","bioguideId":"C001055","cycle":2026,"score":0.005012264412715998,"matches":[{"industry":"utilities-electric","donorAmount":8000,"donorShare":0.010777359053428866,"billConfidence":0.55,"contribution":0.0034867926349328687},{"industry":"energy-renewable","donorAmount":3500,"donorShare":0.004715094585875128,"billConfidence":0.55,"contribution":0.0015254717777831298}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"keyword-fallback","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.6209198669944564},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-7977","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"7977","title":"Energy Bills Relief Act","introducedDate":"2026-03-18","latestActionDate":"2026-03-18","latestActionText":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committees on Agriculture, Ways and Means, Natural Resources, Financial Services, Transportation and Infrastructure, Education and Workforce, Oversight and Government Reform, and Science, Space, and Technology, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committ